  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Developing effective markers for censuring of Sumatran and Javan rhinoceros by local researchers</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to develop microsatellite markers for both Sumatran and Javan rhinoceros species that can effectively be used by Indonesian researchers to census rhino populations, to build capacity of Indonesians with respect to numerous aspects of wildlife genetics including sample collection, DNA extraction, sequencing, genotyping, censusing, analyses, and interpretation of results to compare genomic sequences. This project should further help Indonesian researchers to conduct genetic censusing and sexing of rhinos in local laboratories, in order to monitor and manage their own rhino populations.</narrative>
  </description>
